\u201311), and 4162 (5/bucket). Such hubs manufacture static connectivity by volume; 2644 itself has only 2 events and 2786 only 4 (step_02), with no repeat structure (repeat_ratio 0.005, step_01). Hub co-membership is not cascade evidence, and 2644/3486's activity in [47628,50028] is separated from 2786's by multiple buckets.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_4ac87ef4\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [2644, 2786, 2784, 4697, 41, 3294, 3486, 4162, 1583, 5728],\n  \"window\": [47628, 57228],\n  \"confidence\": 0.62,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"2786 is not within 3 hops of 2644; the only static routes are 5-hop paths. On the path 2644-2784-4697-41-3294-2786, fine-grained bucketing shows 41 is inactive during the bucket when 2786 receives its only early contact, and its 3294 contact falls a bucket later, so the final hop precedes its feeder - ordering is violated and the residual gaps exceed 600 units. The alternative route depends on hub 1583 (~100 events), whose volume explains the static connection without any time-respecting chain. Conclusion: no genuine cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 36752, "total_o